<h2>Three statutes, one obligation</h2>
<p>Indian law approaches a child's maintenance from three directions. The BNSS provides a secular, summary remedy available to children of every community. The HMA allows the matrimonial court to provide for children while deciding the parents' case. HAMA codifies the personal-law obligation of Hindus to maintain their children and aged parents. The obligation is one and the same in substance — a parent with means must support a child who cannot support itself — but the routes differ in scope and machinery.</p>

<table class="law">
